या सन्तुष्ट कर दिया था, इसलिए\nअपने ब्राह्म-तेज से उन्होंने महाराज नाभि को भगवान् नारायण का साक्षात् दर्शन करा दिया।\"\n\nतात्पर्य : यज्ञोत्सव के कार्य में लगे हुए पुरोहित सामान्य ब्राह्मण न थे। वे इतने शक्तिशाली थे कि",
      "textEn": "10\n\nWhose verses are cited by the Pandavas—\nWho is he, O king, who speaks without knowing the consequences? The Lord, who is beyond calamity, is pure in action. 6. Meaning of the word\n\nYasya—Of whom; H—indeed; Pandaveya—that Maharaj Parikshit; Shlokau—two shlokas; Upanishadi—of Upanishads; Anu—by following; Aacharet—\nCould have followed; Puman—Man; Apatyam—Of the son; Agat—Accepted; Yasya—Of whom; Harih—Of God;\nShuddhena—Purely; Karmana—By action; Agam—Accepted; Yasya—Of whom; Harih—Of God;\nShuddhena—Purely; Karmana—By action; Agam—Accepted; Yasya—Of whom; Harih—Of God;\nShuddhena—Purely; Karmana—By action; Agam—Accepted; Yasya—Of whom; Harih—Of God;\nShuddhena—Purely; Karmana—By action; Agam—Accepted; Yasya—Of whom; Harih—Of God; Oh, King Parikshit, in the praise of King Nabhi, ancient sages composed two verses. Among them,\none of these is, \"Oh King, who else can attain a Siddhi like the navel?\" Who can reach their actions? Due to his devotion, God accepted to become his son.\"\n\nMeaning: In this verse, the words 'Shuddhena Karmanam' are important. If any work is not done with devotion,\nthen it becomes contaminated by the qualities of material nature.\nIn the Bhagavad Gita, its explanation\nis given as 'Yajnarthat karmanon yatra loko yatra karmabandhah'. Those actions that are done to please God, only those are pure, and only those are not tainted by the qualities of nature. All other actions\nare contaminated by the qualities of Sattva, Rajas, and Tamas. All the physical actions performed for the satisfaction of the senses are tainted, but Maharaj Nabhi did not perform any such tainted action. Even to the extent that\neven during the time of the Yagya, they had performed divine deeds. Therefore, they attained the form of a son, the Lord. Brahmins, others, where are they, the auspicious ones, worshipped by the nose.\nWhose boon is to show the Yagyesham with the power of Asura. 7. Meaning of the word\n\nBrahmana - a Brahmin devotee; Anya - another; Kutah - where; Nabheha - besides the navel; Vipraha - the Brahmin community;\nMangala-Pujita - well-worshipped and satisfied; Yasya - whose; Barhishi - in the place of sacrifice; Yagya-Isham - the enjoyer of all sacrifices;\nShri Bhagavan; Darshayaam Asu - to show; Ojasa - by one's Brahma power..\n[The second hymn is as follows] \"O King, who can be a worshiper (bhakta) of Brahmins greater than the navel? Because the king had completely satisfied the worthy Brahmins with worship, therefore,\nWith his Brahma-power, he made the Maharaj Nabhi have a direct vision of Lord Narayan.\"\n\nMeaning: The priests engaged in the performance of the Yajna festival were not ordinary Brahmins. They were so powerful that"
