oduce; As—produced. After the departure of Maharaj Nabhi from Badrikashram, the supreme Lord Rishabhdev considered his kingdom as his own field of work. Therefore, he first accepted celibacy under the guidance of the gurus,\nand while presenting his example, he taught the duties of a householder. They also went to reside in the Gurukul. Upon completion of education, they gave Guru Dakshina and then entered Grihasthashrama. He\ntook a wife named Jayanti and produced a hundred sons from her, who were as strong and capable as him.\nAnd worthy. His wife Jayanti was given in marriage by Indra, the king of heavenly hosts. Rishabhdev"
