      "textEn": "110\n\nAll the sons were Kshatriyas by birth, but due to their qualities, some of them became Kshatriyas, while some became Brahmins. Among them, nine sons were preachers of Shrimad Bhagavat (Bhagavata-Dharma-Darshana:) which means that they\nhad risen above the Kshatriya and Brahmin classes. The self-illuminating, self-existent, self-perfecting, and self-sufficient, the only blissful experience, the God himself.\nBeginning with opposite actions, following the time, instructing in the practice of dharma, he is the one who is satisfied with that knowledge.\nCompassionate, endowed with righteousness, fame, and prosperity, he rules the world in houses, in the midst of the obstacles of the mortal world. 14>. Meaning of the word:\n\nBhagavan—Bhagavan; Rishabha—Rishabha; Sanyah—one with name; Atma-tantrah—completely independent; Swayam—self; Nitya—eternal;\nNivritta—detached, liberated; Anartha—of unwanted things (birth, death, old age, and disease); Paramarshah—tradition; Keval—only;\nAnand-anubhava—filled with divine bliss; Ishwarah—God, the controller; Ev—indeed; Prativrutta-vat—like the opposite;\nOf actions—of deeds; beginning—doing; from time—in chronological order; followed—being observed; Dharma—Varna-ashrama Dharma;\nBy conduct—by doing; by teaching—by giving instruction; Un-knowing—ignorant person; Equal—similar; Calmed—by the senses;\nPride—Pride, fame; Praja—Sons and daughters; Bliss—Material happiness; Immortality—Absorption; Obstruction—To attain;\nIn houses—In household life; To the common people—To the general public; Regularized—By making regular. Being an incarnation of the complete Purushottam Bhagwan, Lord Rishabhdev was completely independent because his\nThis form was eternal and divinely blissful. He had no concern with the four laws of physical heat (birth, death,\nold age and disease), nor was he attached to physical vision. They were equals. They were sad seeing others sad. They were the well-wishers of all living beings.\nAlthough they were great\nmen, God, and the Almighty, even then, they were behaving as if they were some ordinary\nbound soul. Therefore, they firmly followed the Varna Ashrama Dharma and performed their duties accordingly. In due course, the rules of the Varna system had become neglected, as a result of which, through their own personal qualities and\nbehavior, they taught the ignorant public to perform their duties under the Varna system. In this\nway, they trained ordinary people in household life so that they could rise religiously and economically,\nand attain fame, progeny, joy, and ultimately eternal life. With his\nteachings, he taught people to become complete while living in the household, while following the rules of the Varna Ashram Dharma. Meaning: Varnaashrama dharma is for those souls who are bound. From this, they attained spiritual progress"
