      "textEn": "116\n\nBy trying to do so, detachment arises from wife, children and home. Then man does not want to waste time. Thus, it becomes self-evident. A person who is advanced in spiritual knowledge\ndoes not engage anyone else in material tasks. The person who cannot save another person through his devotion and teachings is not a part of being a guru, father, mother, deity, or husband. Rishabhdev, while advising his\none hundred sons, advised them to accept their elder brother Bharat as their guide and master. Among all living beings, Brahmins are the best, and Vaishnavas are even better than Brahmins. Serving the Vaishnava means serving Shri Bhagavan. Thus, Shukdev Goswami describes the character of Bharat Maharaj\nand the sacrificial rituals performed by Lord Rishabhdev for the benefit of the general public.\nHe does. Rishabh said,\nHe who does not deserve the body, the body's parts, in this world,\ndoes not deserve the troubles and desires of the world.\nThe divine penance, by which the essence of truth is purified,\nThat which is pure, is the infinite bliss of Brahman. 1. Meaning of the word\n\nRishabhah said—Lord Rishabh said; Na—Not; Ayam—This; Dehaah—Body; Deha-bhājam—Of all embodied beings; Nri-\nLoke—In this world; Kashtan—Distressful; Kamaan—Desire, satisfaction of desires; Arhate—Wanting; Vit-bhumam—Of those who eat excrement; Ye—Those; Tapah—Tapasya; Divyam—Divine; Putrakah—Oh son; Yena—By which; Satvam—Heart; Shuddhayet—Becomes pure; Yasmaat—From whom; Brahma-saṃkhyām—Of the divine bliss; Tu—Certainly; Anantam—Infinite. Lord Rishabhdev said to his sons—O sons, among all the embodied beings in this world, the one who has attained a human body should not work hard day and night only for the satisfaction of the senses.\nBecause even the garbage eaters, the pigs, do that. Man should, to attain the divine position of devotion,\nhe should engage himself in penance.\nBy doing this, his heart becomes pure,\nand when he attains this position, he gets 