ए कि घर पर अर्चाविग्रह की पूजा करे, त्यौहार मनाए, मित्रों को आमंत्रित\nकरे और उन्हें प्रसाद दे। गृहस्थ को इन्हीं कार्यों के लिए धन अर्जित करना चाहिए, इन्द्रियतृप्ति के लिए\nनहीं।",
      "textEn": "120\n\nIn the bodies of men, in the auspicious signs. In houses, in wives, in children,\nNot attached to any purpose in this world. 3. Meaning of words\n\nYe—; Va—; Mayi—; Isha—; Krita-saahrud-arthah—; Janeeshu—; Dehambar-varthikesu—; Griheshu—; Jaya—; Atma-ja—;\nRati—; Matsu—; Na—; Preeti-yuktaah—; Yavat—-arthah—; Cha—; Loke—. Ye—which; Va—or; Mai—me; Isha—in God; Krut-saahrud-arthaah—desiring to increase love (in servitude, friendship,\nin affection or sweetness); Janeshu—in individuals; Deham-bhara-vartikeshu—those who only wish to maintain the body, who have no desire for liberation\n(from worldly existence); Griheshu—in the house; Jaya—wife; Atma-ja—children, offspring; Rati—wealth or friend; Matsu—being associated with; Na—not;\nPriti-yuktaah—extremely attached; Yavat-arthaah—as much as is necessary, living by collecting wealth; Cha—and; Loke—in this material world. Those who are willing to revive Krishna consciousness and increase their love for God, they\ndo not want to do anything that is not related to Shri Krishna.\nThey do not encourage interaction with people who are busy with their body care, food, sleep, sexual activity, and self-defense. They are householders,\neven while being, they are not attached to their household. They are not attached to wife, children, friends, or wealth,\nbut along with that, they do not remain unmindful towards their duties. Such men collect only as much wealth as they need for their livelihood. Meaning: Whether a non-essentialist or a devotee, if he is truly interested in progressing in the self-essence,\nhe should not associate with those who, through the development of so-called civilization,\nshow interest only in maintaining their bodies. Nor should he be eager to enjoy domestic happiness with wife, children, friends, etc. If there is a householder and he has to earn a living, then\nhe should collect only as much wealth as is needed for sustenance. Neither more than this nor\nless than this.\nAs it is said in this verse, a householder should practice Bhakti Yoga—Shravanam Kirtanam\nVishnu's remembrance and service at his feet. Archanam, Vandanam, Dasyam, Sakhyam, Atmanivedanam—to earn money for upbringing,\ntries to do. A householder should lead such a life that they can fully\navoid opportunities for listening and chanting. He should worship the deity at home, celebrate festivals, invite friends,\nand give them prasad. A householder should earn money for these very tasks, not for sensual gratification.\nNo."
